[hermes:err-live] ### pytorch/pytorch#176782 — Fix silent data corruption in triu_/tril_ for expanded tensors
[hermes:err-live] - State: `CLOSED` · Closing-link from PR: no · Source: `hash`
[hermes:err-live] - URL: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/176782
[hermes:err-live] - Author: radeksm
[hermes:err-live] - Labels: triaged, open source, Stale
[hermes:err-live] #### Issue body
[hermes:err-live] Data corruption occurs in `triu_` and `tril_` if the 2D matrix dimensions contain internal memory overlap (e.g. expanding a 0D scalar to a 2D matrix and calling an in-place triangular operation).
[hermes:err-live] By utilizing `at::assert_no_internal_overlap` we avoid false positives on safely broadcasted batch dimensions, the overlap check is applied exclusively to a 2D of a single matrix from the input after batch dimmension was dropped.
[hermes:err-live] This change prevent data corruption and throws **RuntimeError** with message:
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live]   unsupported operation: more than one element of the written-to tensor
[hermes:err-live]   refers to a single memory location. Please clone() the tensor before
[hermes:err-live]   performing the operation.
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] Added positive and negative test scenarios for both `triu_` and `tril_`.
[hermes:err-live] Fixes: #165987
