[review] <!-- torii-review pr=191854 run=local head=9bf17203dbe3dfd1b03ceefa4b12c4385c58acf2 -->
[review] ## 🏴‍☠️ Torii Review — PR #191854
[review] 
[review] **Verdict:** APPROVE
[review] **Confidence:** high
[review] **Score:** 92/100
[review] **Review effort:** 2/5
[review] 
[review] ### Summary
[review] Adds a shared helper `checkTrilTriuMatrixOverlap` that detects internal memory overlap in the last two dimensions of the output tensor for `triu_`/`tril_`, raising `RuntimeError` before silent data corruption occurs. Called from CPU, CUDA, and MPS kernels. Includes a thorough regression test covering overlapping-raise, safe-no-raise, and correctness cases. Clean, minimal, well-targeted fix that builds on the approach explored in #165993 and #176782.
[review] 
[review] ### Walkthrough
[review] - **`TriangularOpsUtils.h`**: New `static inline` helper `checkTrilTriuMatrixOverlap` — early-returns for contiguous or empty tensors, then extracts a 2D view of the last two dims via `as_strided` and delegates to `at::assert_no_internal_overlap`. Also adds `#pragma once` and `#include <ATen/MemoryOverlap.h>`.
[review] - **`TriangularOps.cpp`**: CPU kernel calls `checkTrilTriuMatrixOverlap(result)` after the empty check, before computation.
[review] - **`TriangularOps.cu`**: CUDA kernel calls it at the top of `triu_tril_cu
